1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,270
What if Earth stopped

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:02,007
spinning...

3
00:00:02,027 --> 00:00:03,107
for just one second?

4
00:00:03,807 --> 00:00:04,563
Sounds harmless,

5
00:00:04,563 --> 00:00:05,110
right?

6
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,358
It's one second!

7
00:00:06,378 --> 00:00:07,167
Well...

8
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:08,205
grab a snack.

9
00:00:08,225 --> 00:00:09,124
This is going to get

10
00:00:09,124 --> 00:00:09,407
weird.

11
00:00:12,108 --> 00:00:13,390
First, a confession.

12
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:13,813
Right now,

13
00:00:13,813 --> 00:00:14,598
you are moving.

14
00:00:14,618 --> 00:00:15,282
Fast.

15
00:00:15,302 --> 00:00:16,482
Earth spins once a day,

16
00:00:16,502 --> 00:00:17,712
and at the equator,

17
00:00:17,732 --> 00:00:18,956
the ground beneath you travels

18
00:00:18,956 --> 00:00:21,132
about 1,670 kilometers per

19
00:00:21,132 --> 00:00:21,358
hour.

20
00:00:22,059 --> 00:00:22,901
The farther you are from

21
00:00:22,901 --> 00:00:23,639
the equator,

22
00:00:23,659 --> 00:00:24,888
the slower you go.

23
00:00:24,908 --> 00:00:26,018
New York cruises at about

24
00:00:26,018 --> 00:00:27,348
1,270.

25
00:00:27,368 --> 00:00:29,164
London, about 1,040.

26
00:00:29,184 --> 00:00:30,204
At the North Pole,

27
00:00:30,224 --> 00:00:31,123
you're just turning in a

28
00:00:31,123 --> 00:00:31,858
very slow circle.

29
00:00:32,558 --> 00:00:33,906
And that's just the spin.

30
00:00:33,926 --> 00:00:35,155
Earth also races around the

31
00:00:35,155 --> 00:00:37,021
Sun at about 107,000

32
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:38,076
kilometers per hour,

33
00:00:38,096 --> 00:00:39,048
while the Sun drags us

34
00:00:39,048 --> 00:00:40,696
around the galaxy even faster.

35
00:00:40,716 --> 00:00:42,488
Relax: nobody is stopping

36
00:00:42,488 --> 00:00:42,997
those.

37
00:00:43,017 --> 00:00:43,416
Today.

38
00:00:44,116 --> 00:00:44,977
So why don't you feel

39
00:00:44,977 --> 00:00:45,374
it?

40
00:00:45,394 --> 00:00:46,671
Because everything moves with

41
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:48,024
you: the ground,

42
00:00:48,024 --> 00:00:48,366
the air,

43
00:00:48,366 --> 00:00:49,156
the oceans.

44
00:00:49,176 --> 00:00:50,518
It's like a smooth flight.

45
00:00:50,538 --> 00:00:51,339
You can sip coffee at

46
00:00:51,339 --> 00:00:53,519
900 km/h without spilling a

47
00:00:53,519 --> 00:00:53,831
drop.

48
00:00:54,531 --> 00:00:55,983
You already know this feeling.

49
00:00:56,003 --> 00:00:57,253
When a bus brakes hard,

50
00:00:57,273 --> 00:00:58,259
you lurch forward.

51
00:00:58,279 --> 00:00:59,329
That's inertia:

52
00:00:59,349 --> 00:01:00,526
moving things keep moving

53
00:01:00,526 --> 00:01:01,971
until something stops them.

54
00:01:01,991 --> 00:01:03,078
Now imagine the bus is

55
00:01:03,078 --> 00:01:04,221
the entire planet.

56
00:01:04,241 --> 00:01:06,067
And it's doing 1,670.

57
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:07,915
Now, the experiment.

58
00:01:07,935 --> 00:01:08,705
Without warning,

59
00:01:08,725 --> 00:01:09,647
the planet slams on the

60
00:01:09,647 --> 00:01:10,236
brakes.

61
00:01:10,256 --> 00:01:11,179
Earth stops.

62
00:01:11,199 --> 00:01:11,878
You don't.

63
00:01:11,898 --> 00:01:12,911
Neither does the air.

64
00:01:12,931 --> 00:01:14,070
Or the oceans.

65
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:15,042
Or that sandwich you were

66
00:01:15,042 --> 00:01:15,432
holding.

67
00:01:16,132 --> 00:01:17,187
Half a heartbeat later,

68
00:01:17,187 --> 00:01:18,287
you're hurtling east at about

69
00:01:18,287 --> 00:01:19,430
Mach 1.4.

70
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:20,622
That's faster than the speed

71
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:21,322
of sound.

72
00:01:21,342 --> 00:01:22,442
In that one second,

73
00:01:22,462 --> 00:01:25,242
you'd cover 465 meters:

74
00:01:25,262 --> 00:01:26,183
about four and a half

75
00:01:26,183 --> 00:01:26,885
football pitches.

76
00:01:27,584 --> 00:01:28,484
The good news:

77
00:01:28,504 --> 00:01:29,720
you won't fly for long.

78
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:30,622
Gravity pulls you to the

79
00:01:30,622 --> 00:01:31,589
ground in about half a

80
00:01:31,589 --> 00:01:32,145
second.

81
00:01:32,165 --> 00:01:33,185
The bad news:

82
00:01:33,205 --> 00:01:34,556
you land moving almost twice

83
00:01:34,556 --> 00:01:35,457
as fast as a cruising

84
00:01:35,457 --> 00:01:35,947
jet.

85
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:36,801
Sideways.

86
00:01:36,821 --> 00:01:37,929
Into everything that just

87
00:01:37,929 --> 00:01:38,517
stopped.

88
00:01:38,537 --> 00:01:39,516
Which is...

89
00:01:39,536 --> 00:01:40,035
everything.

90
00:01:40,735 --> 00:01:42,163
Wait, would you fly off

91
00:01:42,163 --> 00:01:43,185
into space?

92
00:01:43,205 --> 00:01:43,695
Nope.

93
00:01:43,715 --> 00:01:44,888
To escape Earth's gravity

94
00:01:44,888 --> 00:01:46,418
you'd need about 40,000

95
00:01:46,418 --> 00:01:47,607
kilometers per hour.

96
00:01:47,627 --> 00:01:48,569
You're doing barely four

97
00:01:48,569 --> 00:01:49,448
percent of that.

98
00:01:49,468 --> 00:01:50,701
So you stay on Earth.

99
00:01:50,721 --> 00:01:51,509
Unfortunately.

100
00:01:52,209 --> 00:01:53,402
And it's not just you.

101
00:01:53,422 --> 00:01:54,492
Cars, trains,

102
00:01:54,512 --> 00:01:55,074
rocks, cows.

103
00:01:55,094 --> 00:01:56,410
Everything that isn't bolted

104
00:01:56,410 --> 00:01:57,531
down takes the same trip

105
00:01:57,531 --> 00:01:57,823
east.

106
00:01:58,523 --> 00:01:59,576
Then there's the air.

107
00:01:59,596 --> 00:02:00,861
The whole atmosphere keeps

108
00:02:00,861 --> 00:02:01,905
rushing east at up to

109
00:02:01,905 --> 00:02:04,710
1,670 kilometers per hour.

110
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:05,901
That's more than three times

111
00:02:05,901 --> 00:02:06,926
faster than the strongest

112
00:02:06,926 --> 00:02:08,512
tornado winds ever measured.

113
00:02:08,532 --> 00:02:09,764
Except this tornado is the

114
00:02:09,764 --> 00:02:10,617
size of a planet.

115
00:02:11,317 --> 00:02:12,919
The oceans keep going too.

116
00:02:12,939 --> 00:02:14,258
Water sloshes east and piles

117
00:02:14,258 --> 00:02:15,484
up against the western coasts

118
00:02:15,484 --> 00:02:16,779
of every continent,

119
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:18,507
in walls of tsunami-sized

120
00:02:18,507 --> 00:02:19,171
waves.

121
00:02:19,191 --> 00:02:20,649
Somewhere, a surfer is having

122
00:02:20,649 --> 00:02:21,588
the best and worst day

123
00:02:21,588 --> 00:02:22,104
of their life.

124
00:02:22,804 --> 00:02:23,743
So who gets through this

125
00:02:23,743 --> 00:02:24,536
just fine?

126
00:02:24,556 --> 00:02:25,334
Astronauts on the

127
00:02:25,334 --> 00:02:26,836
International Space Station.

128
00:02:26,856 --> 00:02:27,925
They orbit Earth instead of

129
00:02:27,925 --> 00:02:28,530
riding on it,

130
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:29,135
so for them,

131
00:02:29,135 --> 00:02:30,344
it's just a very strange

132
00:02:30,344 --> 00:02:30,843
view.

133
00:02:30,863 --> 00:02:31,919
People at the poles barely

134
00:02:31,919 --> 00:02:32,689
move at all.

135
00:02:32,709 --> 00:02:34,319
Penguins are mostly fine too,

136
00:02:34,339 --> 00:02:35,428
though they don't actually

137
00:02:35,428 --> 00:02:36,596
live at the South Pole.

138
00:02:36,616 --> 00:02:37,719
And pilots?

139
00:02:37,739 --> 00:02:38,949
Their planes already fly with

140
00:02:38,949 --> 00:02:39,960
the air around them.

141
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:40,860
For one second,

142
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:41,961
nothing changes up there.

143
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:43,619
Now the twist.

144
00:02:43,639 --> 00:02:44,236
The second is over,

145
00:02:44,236 --> 00:02:45,008
and Earth starts spinning

146
00:02:45,008 --> 00:02:46,498
again, instantly.

147
00:02:46,518 --> 00:02:47,863
Anything still flying east is

148
00:02:47,863 --> 00:02:49,008
suddenly back in sync with

149
00:02:49,008 --> 00:02:49,726
the ground.

150
00:02:49,746 --> 00:02:50,395
Lucky.

151
00:02:50,415 --> 00:02:51,397
But everything that crashed

152
00:02:51,397 --> 00:02:52,294
and stopped during that

153
00:02:52,294 --> 00:02:52,915
second?

154
00:02:52,935 --> 00:02:54,204
The ground races back under

155
00:02:54,204 --> 00:02:55,186
it at full speed.

156
00:02:55,206 --> 00:02:56,474
So the whole disaster happens

157
00:02:56,474 --> 00:02:57,117
again...

158
00:02:57,137 --> 00:02:58,075
in the other direction.

159
00:02:58,775 --> 00:03:00,128
Physics would like a word.

160
00:03:00,148 --> 00:03:01,307
Earth's spin stores about

161
00:03:01,307 --> 00:03:03,945
2×10²⁹ joules of energy.

162
00:03:03,965 --> 00:03:05,269
Stopping it means dumping all

163
00:03:05,269 --> 00:03:06,165
of that somewhere.

164
00:03:06,185 --> 00:03:07,197
That's roughly what the Sun

165
00:03:07,197 --> 00:03:08,670
pours out in nine minutes.

166
00:03:08,690 --> 00:03:09,359
All of the Sun.

167
00:03:10,059 --> 00:03:11,258
And if Earth never started

168
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:11,850
again?

169
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:12,845
One day would last a

170
00:03:12,845 --> 00:03:13,552
whole year.

171
00:03:13,572 --> 00:03:15,022
Six months of daylight,

172
00:03:15,042 --> 00:03:16,347
then six months of night.

173
00:03:16,367 --> 00:03:17,240
And the Sun would rise

174
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:17,993
in the west.

175
00:03:18,013 --> 00:03:18,623
Over time,

176
00:03:18,643 --> 00:03:19,636
the oceans would migrate

177
00:03:19,636 --> 00:03:20,593
toward the poles,

178
00:03:20,613 --> 00:03:21,849
leaving one giant continent

179
00:03:21,849 --> 00:03:22,797
wrapped around the equator.

180
00:03:23,498 --> 00:03:24,688
Here's the wild part:

181
00:03:24,708 --> 00:03:25,598
Earth's spin really does

182
00:03:25,598 --> 00:03:27,434
change, just a tiny bit.

183
00:03:27,454 --> 00:03:28,798
Tides, earthquakes and melting

184
00:03:28,798 --> 00:03:29,530
ice nudge the length of

185
00:03:29,530 --> 00:03:30,767
a day by milliseconds.

186
00:03:30,787 --> 00:03:31,917
In 2020,

187
00:03:31,937 --> 00:03:33,018
Earth even clocked some of

188
00:03:33,018 --> 00:03:34,005
its shortest days ever

189
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:34,554
measured.

190
00:03:34,574 --> 00:03:35,834
To keep clocks honest,

191
00:03:35,854 --> 00:03:37,692
scientists have added 27 leap

192
00:03:37,692 --> 00:03:39,993
seconds since 1972.

193
00:03:40,013 --> 00:03:40,971
And they plan to stop

194
00:03:40,971 --> 00:03:42,423
by 2035,

195
00:03:42,443 --> 00:03:43,626
partly because leap seconds

196
00:03:43,626 --> 00:03:44,852
keep confusing computers.

197
00:03:45,552 --> 00:03:46,716
So, could Earth stop spinning

198
00:03:46,716 --> 00:03:47,712
for one second?

199
00:03:47,732 --> 00:03:48,217
No.

200
00:03:48,237 --> 00:03:49,099
Nothing we know of could

201
00:03:49,099 --> 00:03:50,497
brake a planet that fast.

202
00:03:50,517 --> 00:03:51,387
But if it did,

203
00:03:51,407 --> 00:03:52,597
the stop would be bad,

204
00:03:52,617 --> 00:03:53,581
and the restart would be

205
00:03:53,581 --> 00:03:54,065
worse.

206
00:03:54,085 --> 00:03:55,155
On the bright side,

207
00:03:55,175 --> 00:03:56,187
you'd have the best excuse

208
00:03:56,187 --> 00:03:57,293
ever for being late.

209
00:03:57,313 --> 00:03:58,475
Hold on to your sandwich.

210
00:03:59,776 --> 00:04:00,877
That's one second you'll never

211
00:04:00,877 --> 00:04:01,492
get back.

212
00:04:01,512 --> 00:04:02,583
Spend the next five minutes

213
00:04:02,583 --> 00:04:03,332
on another what-if,

214
00:04:03,352 --> 00:04:04,012
right here.

215
00:04:04,032 --> 00:04:04,813
And if you want Bix

216
00:04:04,813 --> 00:04:05,810
to break more planets,

217
00:04:05,810 --> 00:04:06,507
subscribe.

218
00:04:06,527 --> 00:04:07,216
Responsibly.
